; Storage on a diskette, for a Project whose Container is the `d64`: the tracks
; of a 1541's surface as units, the driver that reads them, and the decoders the
; tool ships.
;
; A unit is a **track** and its number is the track's, so unit zero is no track
; and unit 18 is the directory; neither is ever allocated. `size` is the widest
; track and therefore a **stride**, not a size — what a narrower track does not
; have is held against every image, which is safe because the driver is promised
; that nothing crosses a unit. The two numbers are checked against the Container
; (`NGA1238`), since a driver handed a unit of the wrong width would read the
; wrong bytes with nothing to say so. See docs/spec/d64.md.
;
; A Project includes this beside `pet/3032.ngp`.
storage { units 36  size 5376 }

modules { "pet/disk.asm"  "stream/zx0.asm" }
resident { disk, zx0 }
